{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem","id":1008317,"title":"Dracula's powers in Requiem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-25T16:23:13-08:00","id":1008317,"title":"Dracula's powers in Requiem","content":"As corresponding with the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1006849-the-powers-of-dracula-or-the-traditional-vampire-in-vtm\">Masquerade counterpart thread</a>, what are the disciplines in Requiem that can exactly replicate the powers described in Bram Stoker's Dracula and also future adaptions like Castlevania and such? Especially trying to match the aesthetics of the Dracula style or &quot;traditional&quot; vampire like cloud of bats, wolf, mist, glowing red eyes, pale skin, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T16:36:31-08:00","id":1008321,"title":"","content":"I don't know about Castlevania, but...<br /> <br /> Protean lets you: manifest beast traits, change into beasts, and it lets you shift into a cloud of bloody mist. (Take the Swarm merit to do clouds of bats.)<br /> Dominate/majesty to get you the power of seducing a grand total of three bride's and some poor sob's future wife.<br /> Mystery of the Ascedant to do the daywalker thing a bit better.<br /> <br /> What else is there... Pale skin: just never use Blush of Life.<br /> Red eyes: this could be a Bane or you could choose to be a Nosferatu and have the glowing monster goggles be a manifestation of your Clan's curse.<br /> <br /> EDIT: 's been a while since I read Stoker, but wikipedia tells me you'd also need:<br /> - super strength, which is gained of course by buying up points in Vigor<br /> - crawling walls can be done with Protean<br /> - flight, can be done with Protean. Levitation, not as written. But a custom Devotion might take care of that.<br /> - there is mention of a sailor trying to stab the Count with a knife, but the knife passes through the monster's body. This can be explained via Celerity or a Devotional refinement of the 5th Protean power<br /> - traveling to unhallowed grounds. Auspex 5 devotion.<br /> - telepathy: straight up Auspex 4.<br /> - illusions: obfuscate and/or nightmare<br /> - some kind of teleportation-ish escape act... Quite difficult. Can't just be remedied with Celerity. In VtR 1e there was a Boodline called the Carnival if I am not mistaken. Contortionist licks. They might help you out here.<br /> - command animals: Animalism<br /> - manipulating the weather... Bloodmagic, probably Cruac","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","user":"Howalt","date":". 11-25-2016, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:05:05-08:00","id":1008326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008321#post1008321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Red eyes: this could be a Bane or you could choose to be a Nosferatu and have the glowing monster goggles be a manifestation of your Clan's curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well what about having red eyes as a Daeva?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008321#post1008321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- some kind of teleportation-ish escape act... Quite difficult. Can't just be remedied with Celerity. In VtR 1e there was a Boodline called the Carnival if I am not mistaken. Contortionist licks. They might help you out here.<br /> - manipulating the weather... Bloodmagic, probably Cruac</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe at this point this is the other reason why some disciplines from Masquerade like Thaumaturgy and Koldunism needs to be imported? Oh Dracula is also capable of Necromancy and also in Francis Cord Coppla's Dracula he also has Obtenebration...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:36:06-08:00","id":1008335,"title":"","content":"Red eyes as a Daeva? Get punched in the eyes real hard. As in: get subconjunctival hemmorages all over them. Spend Willpower to make these &quot;scars&quot; permanent. Heal the mechanical damage. Done.<br /> <br /> I don't see why things from Masquerade need to be imported. I'm vaguely aware of Thaumaturgy, I think you can replicate most of that using blood magics. You can definetly manipulate the weather using bloodmagic in VtR 1e, IIRC the Bloodsorcery supplement has rules for this. All you need to do is port those to 2e.<br /> <br /> I looked up the Carnival bloodline, you can easily transform the relevant powers from their Discipline, the Show, into Protean devotions for escape act purposes. Combine with Celerity to creatae a Devotion that gives the impression of teleportation.<br /> <br /> I don't remember Gary Oldman, raising the dead. But if you say so. There is a standard possibility for post-mortem Embrace in VtR 2e, though I suspect that's not what you're looking for. You might want to check out that Bloodsorcery supplement again, though. Really.<br /> <br /> Try to not think in terms of Masquerade when reading through VtR is, I think, an advice you might benefit from on the whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","user":"Howalt","date":". 11-25-2016, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:41:56-08:00","id":1008336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008335#post1008335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Red eyes as a Daeva? Get punched in the eyes real hard. As in: get subconjunctival hemmorages all over them. Spend Willpower to make these &quot;scars&quot; permanent. Heal the mechanical damage. Done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonono....<br /> <br /> I actually mean a supernatural trait of red glowing eyes (or blood shot eyes) as a Daeva if they're capable picking up that. Not that....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-25-2016, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:47:12-08:00","id":1008338,"title":"","content":"Glowing eyes are kind of a Strix thing in Requiem. Although if you want red ones you need to go with the Japanese variety mentioned in Werewolf: the Forsaken. <br /> <br /> Honestly I've always pegged Dracula as a Gangrel anyway. Dude definitely likes his Protean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:47:41-08:00","id":1008339,"title":"","content":"These are literal blood shot eyes. Quite supernatural too, as they are permanently present. Still, you want something else: I think you could just eat a one of those white-haired, red-eyed lab rats. That way you could manifest those beady vermilion stargazers using Protean. An ST might allow you to spend WP to make the change permanent. For a glow effect: manifest a tapetum lucidum, again using Protean. This is the stuff that makes your cat's eyes shine in the dark. Spend WP to make the change permanent, if allowed by your ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:51:59-08:00","id":1008344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008338#post1008338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glowing eyes are kind of a Strix thing in Requiem. Although if you want red ones you need to go with the Japanese variety mentioned in Werewolf: the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>However this is not what I'm looking for since this is a playable Vampire character we're talking about here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008338#post1008338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I've always pegged Dracula as a Gangrel anyway. Dude definitely likes his Protean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt Dracula is gangrel just because he uses Protean since any clan can learn and use it. Plus I highly suspect that Dracula from VtR lore might be clanless anyways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008339#post1008339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are literal blood shot eyes. Quite supernatural too, as they are permanently present. Still, you want something else: I think you could just eat a one of those white-haired, red-eyed lab rats. That way you could manifest those beady vermilion stargazers using Protean. An ST might allow you to spend WP to make the change permanent. For a glow effect: manifest a tapetum lucidum, again using Protean. This is the stuff that makes your cat's eyes shine in the dark. Spend WP to make the change permanent, if allowed by your ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also not what I'm looking for since what I'm thinking of they're more like either supernatural cosmetics or passed down from a particular sire and their childer happens to carry it, Although I'm also open to the non-permanant ones like most of the time they their normal normal eye color but able to switch it to crimson red like a on/off switch when they feel like it.<br /> <br /> Well here's a more literal picture I'm thinking of: <a href=\"http://www.deviantart.com/art/Sonja-Blue-272744902\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.deviantart.com/art/Sonja-Blue-272744902</a><br /> <br /> Well imagine their eyes glowing like that and they have to wear &quot;Sunglasses at midnight&quot; to cover them up....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-25-2016, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:00:03-08:00","id":1008348,"title":"","content":"Wait, I just remembered, it's one of the banes you can take to avoid humanity loss:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Face of Hunger:</b> When your character finds himself hungry,<br /> it shows on his face and on his skin. His eyes grow red, and his<br /> skin pulls tight over his visage. He looks every bit the corpse.<br /> When he has less than five Vitae, his Humanity dots act as a<br /> cap on all his Social actions. Humanity also caps all dice pools<br /> to resist frenzy inspired by hunger. </div> </div> </div>Ok, so it doesn't say their eyes <i>glow</i>, but that's a minor cosmetic tweak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:01:43-08:00","id":1008349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008348#post1008348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so it doesn't say their eye's <i>glow</i>, but that's a minor cosmetic tweak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course I kinda want them to glow....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:04:36-08:00","id":1008350,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I meant you can just say Dracula has a bit of an over-dramatic version of the bane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:58:24-08:00","id":1008366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008349#post1008349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course I kinda want them to glow....</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every little detail has to be spelled out in a book for it to possible for your character.<br /> <br /> Just ask the ST about it. It's just a cosmetic detail, one that will make your life way harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:58:32-08:00","id":1008367,"title":"","content":"If glowing eyes is that important to you, and you don't think the face of hunger Bane is sufficient, you can just make a custom Bane that does it, or a Bloodline that has it as a weakness, or a Merit that has it as a drawback or something. Like, you have such a specific effect in mind, might as well just make it instead of trying to shoehorn something that doesn't fit your needs.<br /> <br /> Also, re: Dracula's Clan, it's all but canon that he's Gangrel. The big bald bearded dude in the Gangrel chapter? That's his Grandchilde, or at least claims to be. Requiem's take aside, Stoker's Dracula had so much werewolf imagery conflated with the vampire imagery, and such a strong feral/animalistic vibe, there's no question in my mind that he would be anything but Gangrel, even before considering his mastery of Protean and talent for Animalism. Just cause he was charismatic doesn't mean he has to have been Daeva.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-25-2016, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T19:26:33-08:00","id":1008378,"title":"","content":"Reighnhell wrote <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=746399#post746399\"><b>stats for Dracula</b></a> a while ago, and I think they're pretty spot on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T19:35:34-08:00","id":1008383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008367#post1008367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If glowing eyes is that important to you, and you don't think the face of hunger Bane is sufficient, you can just make a custom Bane that does it, or a Bloodline that has it as a weakness, or a Merit that has it as a drawback or something. Like, you have such a specific effect in mind, might as well just make it instead of trying to shoehorn something that doesn't fit your needs.<br /> <br /> Also, re: Dracula's Clan, it's all but canon that he's Gangrel. The big bald bearded dude in the Gangrel chapter? That's his Grandchilde, or at least claims to be. Requiem's take aside, Stoker's Dracula had so much werewolf imagery conflated with the vampire imagery, and such a strong feral/animalistic vibe, there's no question in my mind that he would be anything but Gangrel, even before considering his mastery of Protean and talent for Animalism. Just cause he was charismatic doesn't mean he has to have been Daeva.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry but not only I have a hard time imagining him being Gangrel but also I just don't like that idea, it takes away the mystery of who he actually is which is why I prefer him to be clanless. Even in Masquerade he was a Tzimisce which was more appropriate.<br /> <br /> Just because he masters Protean doesn't mean he's a Gangrel.<br /> <br /> Also Vlad Dracul is more from a noble class since Gangrel are geared towards Peasants and Backwoods people (and in modern times, bikers, gangbangers, or anyone from working class or lumpenproletariat background, etc) which is how I view Gangrel well especially during that time and it's very unlikely that a Gangrel would embrace someone from Royal/Noble blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-25-2016, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T19:48:20-08:00","id":1008385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008383#post1008383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry but not only I have a hard time imagining him being Gangrel but also I just don't like that idea, it takes away the mystery of who he actually is which is why I prefer him to be clanless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, ain't nothing wrong with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008383#post1008383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in Masquerade he was a Tzimisce which was more appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was more appropriate in Masquerade, where Tzimisice were a thing that existed and Gangrel were the Clan of dudes who look like animals and live in the woods. But as we've discussed in other threads, Requiem is not Masquerade. The Clan of the Savages is not the Clan of the Outsiders despite them sharing the same name, and there is no Clan of the Fiends to be found in Requiem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008383#post1008383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because he masters Protean doesn't mean he's a Gangrel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and Protean is probably the least of the reasons Requiem Gangrel suit him well (in my opinion, obviously). As I said, it has more to do with the werewolf imagery and the feral attitude. Seriously, Stoker's Dracula was <i>super</i> animalistic, and not just because he could turn into and control animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T19:56:19-08:00","id":1008387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008385#post1008385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, Stoker's Dracula was <i>super</i> animalistic, and not just because he could turn into and control animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think reason for Dracula being super animalistic in the book had more to do with deeply seething caricaturist or rather racist polemics against foreigners or &quot;The Other&quot; who were 'taking away their women' which is what Dracula originally represented which was sadly common in the late Victorian era, well just like F.W. Mernau's &quot;Nosferatu&quot; suspiciously looks like a anti-semetic caricature especially being associated with Rats and Plagues which was also common anti-semetic imagery at the time (oh even the whole &quot;burning in sunlight&quot; death concept from it which I highly suspect is also anti-semetic imagery as well if you really think about it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-25-2016, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T20:25:25-08:00","id":1008394,"title":"","content":"While reading 2ed with all of its hints about Strix creating the first vampires and the actual rules for Strix possession of vampires and the living the thought occurred to me of having a vampire that wasn't part of a bloodline but was created when a Strix possession went a little skewampus, creating a hybrid or dual natured being that resembles a vampire but isn't the same as the clans.<br /> \u200bYou could even portray his shadow acting out his purely Strix desires on the wall behind him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T20:39:22-08:00","id":1008396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008387#post1008387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think reason for Dracula being super animalistic in the book had more to do with deeply seething caricaturist or rather racist polemics against foreigners or &quot;The Other&quot; who were 'taking away their women' which is what Dracula originally represented which was sadly common in the late Victorian era, well just like F.W. Mernau's &quot;Nosferatu&quot; suspiciously looks like a anti-semetic caricature especially being associated with Rats and Plagues which was also common anti-semetic imagery at the time (oh even the whole &quot;burning in sunlight&quot; death concept from it which I highly suspect is also anti-semetic imagery as well if you really think about it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is accurate. It's still a part of his character, which places him pretty solidly as Gangrel in my mind, just like Orloch is solidly Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> Also, in response to your earlier edit, which I didn't see before:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008383#post1008383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Vlad Dracul is more from a noble class since Gangrel are geared towards Peasants and Backwoods people (and in modern times, bikers, gangbangers, or anyone from working class or lumpenproletariat background, etc) which is how I view Gangrel well especially during that time and it's very unlikely that a Gangrel would embrace someone from Royal/Noble blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clans aren't that particular in what &quot;stock&quot; they embrace from in Requiem. That's a Masquerade thing. Gangrel in Requiem can quite easily be upper class, even noble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-25-2016, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T21:45:31-08:00","id":1008410,"title":"","content":"Also remember that Dracula wasn't a noble dancing in Louis the XIV's court, he was more of a backwoods warlord who spent his mortal life fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T09:13:07-08:00","id":1008573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008367#post1008367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If glowing eyes is that important to you, and you don't think the face of hunger Bane is sufficient, you can just make a custom Bane that does it, or a Bloodline that has it as a weakness, or a Merit that has it as a drawback or something. Like, you have such a specific effect in mind, might as well just make it instead of trying to shoehorn something that doesn't fit your needs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively: his eyes could flare red if and when he chooses to Lash Out<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T10:28:06-08:00","id":1008597,"title":"","content":"For levitation, you could just do the wing thing with Protean, and then hide them with obfuscate. People close to you will still feel the wind in their faces, but for all they know you might as well have an invisible helicopter rotor like Inspector Gadget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T10:37:47-08:00","id":1008603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>S. Brechen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008597#post1008597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For levitation, you could just do the wing thing with Protean, and then hide them with obfuscate. People close to you will still feel the wind in their faces, but for all they know you might as well have an invisible helicopter rotor like Inspector Gadget.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's too much though which is why I think there should be a levitation power without going through all that trouble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008396#post1008396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clans aren't that particular in what &quot;stock&quot; they embrace from in Requiem. That's a Masquerade thing. Gangrel in Requiem can quite easily be upper class, even noble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again though, this is only assuming if the events of the book even happened at all since in Masquerade, Vlad just had Stoker write the novel but I'm not so sure if it's the same in Requiem.<br /> <br /> Well the point is, the Dracula from the book may not be the same Vlad Dracul that founded the Ordo Dracul assuming the events of Stoker's novel were fictional. Although Vlad Dracul may some similarities like his powers/weaknesses and maybe he did visited Victorian London but under a different circumstance than it happened in the book.<br /> <br /> I just prefer Dracula not to be of any clan at all but rather he's a Progenitor like Longinus (since it's possible that Progenitor vampires have greater immense powers than normal Kindred so anything is 'possible' with them which is how Dracula himself invented the coils in the first place) and whoever spawned the original Kindred before them which maybe Lilith or someone inspired by her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 11-26-2016, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T10:56:42-08:00","id":1008611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008387#post1008387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think reason for Dracula being super animalistic in the book had more to do with deeply seething caricaturist or rather racist polemics against foreigners or &quot;The Other&quot; who were 'taking away their women' which is what Dracula originally represented which was sadly common in the late Victorian era, well just like F.W. Mernau's &quot;Nosferatu&quot; suspiciously looks like a anti-semetic caricature especially being associated with Rats and Plagues which was also common anti-semetic imagery at the time (oh even the whole &quot;burning in sunlight&quot; death concept from it which I highly suspect is also anti-semetic imagery as well if you really think about it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Those may have been conscious or unconscious influences on the originals, but I don't think that requires us to always have to view those characteristics through the lens of &quot;racist caricature.&quot; Dracula could just as easily be reinterpreted as representing predatory sexuality, or the Id in general. The Requiem clans are broad enough that they read as analogues for what Freud would refer to as <i>thanatoi, </i>those things that we know can destroy us but we long for regardless. The Masquerade clans were far more &quot;ethnic,&quot; which could a little tactless at times. <br /> <br /> In the book, Dracula isn't really plotting to take over the world, or looking for a mortal to make his lover. He's an old, tired monster who senses that his time is running out, so he's going to get a change of scenery for a change, and cause as much mayhem as he can before he goes down fighting. That's Gangrel AF in my book. <br /> <br /> And if you're still having trouble imagining him as a Gangrel, take a look at some of the bloodlines. Want to focus on his depiction as a nobleman who treats his land as his territory, and his subjects as prey? Take a look at the Annunaku. Want to focus on him being the ancient, aged menace living on the fringes of civilization? He's an Oberloch. Want to channel the sex symbol depiction? Maybe he's a Kerberos, trying to transition from Medieval nobleman to Victorian gentleman. <br /> <br /> The point is, the clans are broad enough that you can get a lot of mileage out of each one, and end up with some pretty diverse characters and concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T11:14:25-08:00","id":1008617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008603#post1008603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's too much though which is why I think there should be a levitation power without going through all that trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you create a levitation power (either through Devotions or Bloodmagics) it should still require quite a bit of trouble (i.e. XP) to get. It's quite an ability, you see. Besides Dracula probably has gone through a lot of trouble to get where he is tonight. Also, I take it that you're building him as an NPC, not as a PC. So it doesn't matter all that much how many Experiences it requires to fill out his sheet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008603#post1008603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again though, this is only assuming if the events of the book even happened at all since in Masquerade, Vlad just had Stoker write the novel but I'm not so sure if it's the same in Requiem.<br /> <br /> Well the point is, the Dracula from the book may not be the same Vlad Dracul that founded the Ordo Dracul assuming the events of Stoker's novel were fictional. Although Vlad Dracul may some similarities like his powers/weaknesses and maybe he did visited Victorian London but under a different circumstance than it happened in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is confusing; you asked for Disciplines/Devotions/Sorceries to cover the Dracula <i>as described by Stoker</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008603#post1008603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I just prefer Dracula not to be of any clan at all but rather he's a Progenitor like Longinus (since it's possible that Progenitor vampires have greater immense powers than normal Kindred so anything is 'possible' with them which is how Dracula himself invented the coils in the first place) and whoever spawned the original Kindred before them which maybe Lilith or someone inspired by her.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Longinus was necessarily more powerful than your average neonate when he first arose as a Kindred. I don't think this is the case with Dracula either. The dude just worked his ass of is all (i.e. he gathered a shit ton of XP).<br /> <br /> If you prefer him clanless, that's fine. But your preference doesn't change the fact that if Vlad <i>were</i> to have a Clan, Gangrel would be the most obvious choice. It also doesn't change the fact that, as far as canon may be said to exist in this game, in Requiem mr. Tepes was probably turned into a Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","user":"Howalt","date":". 11-26-2016, 02:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T11:20:46-08:00","id":1008619,"title":"","content":"As a mention, Rites of the Dragon posits, of course, that Dracula is Clanless, but most of the time his powers seem to align with the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> This of course assumes you are running with the canon on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T11:31:14-08:00","id":1008626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008619#post1008619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a mention, Rites of the Dragon posits, of course, that Dracula is Clanless, but most of the time his powers seem to align with the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> This of course assumes you are running with the canon on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>PURE ideology. /Sniffles<br /> <br /> But yeah, thanks for that note. Almost forgot about it, tbh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T11:34:57-08:00","id":1008629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008603#post1008603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's too much though which is why I think there should be a levitation power without going through all that trouble.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. Just make a Devotion. Or a Cruac ritual. Or a Bloodline with a Gift that grants levitation. What ever you want.<br /> <br /> You have a lot of very specific ideas about what powers you think should exist in Requiem. So just make them. It's meant to be a toolbox. Storytellers are actively encouraged to create custom material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008603#post1008603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again though, this is only assuming if the events of the book even happened at all since in Masquerade, Vlad just had Stoker write the novel but I'm not so sure if it's the same in Requiem.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not. In Requiem, the advent of Stoker's novel created quite a stir in the Kindred community due to how shockingly accurate it was. There is a great deal of speculation as to whether Stoker was a hunter or a ghoul or something, or more likely had an informant who was. The specific events of the novel were <i>probably</i> fictional, but the details about Dracula were mostly correct. Most likely it was a clever way to spread awareness about vampires, and about Dracula in particular. It ended up doing more good for the Kindred than harm though, as it didn't end up destroying the Masquerade,but it did spark a rise in interest regarding Dracula in the Kindred community and drove a huge spike in open Ordo Dracul membership.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008603#post1008603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the point is, the Dracula from the book may not be the same Vlad Dracul that founded the Ordo Dracul assuming the events of Stoker's novel were fictional. Although Vlad Dracul may some similarities like his powers/weaknesses and maybe he did visited Victorian London but under a different circumstance than it happened in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if we're talking about Requiem's Dracula, there is strong evidence of him being Gangrel. Apart from the fact that his fictional counterpart bore an uncanny resemblance to the genuine article, his (alleged) grandchilde is literally the poster boy for the Clan. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1008317-dracula-s-powers-in-requiem?p=1008603#post1008603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just prefer Dracula not to be of any clan at all but rather he's a Progenitor like Longinus (since it's possible that Progenitor vampires have greater immense powers than normal Kindred so anything is 'possible' with them which is how Dracula himself invented the coils in the first place) and whoever spawned the original Kindred before them which maybe Lilith or someone inspired by her.</div> </div> </div> </div>From what we learn in Rites of the Dragon, he claims to have no Clan, and to have been spontaneously embrace. <i>If</i> we take Rites of the Dragon at face value, then he was definitely something beyond ordinary Kindred. However, Of course, we only have his word to go on, and that's assuming he even actually existed and the Rites of the Dragon was actually written by him.The account of the battle preceeding his embrace does strongly indicate the possibility of a (possibly unintended) postmortem embrace by his opponent, who could have been of any Clan. And even if his Embrace was spontaneous, and even if he actually possessed all of his alleged abilities, that still doesn't necessarily mean he is above Clan. He could well just be a superlative example of his Clan - a unique Bloodline, or some unspecified deviation of the blood. So, there is ample reason to doubt his claims. And if you prefer him Clanless, there is ample support for that interpretation as well. But <i>if</i> he belonged to any Clan, there is stronger evidence for it having been Gangrel than any other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 11-26-2016, 02:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T12:54:44-08:00","id":1008650,"title":"","content":"I had an idea I used in my last campaign for (sort of) clanless vampires. One way to interpret the strix is that they might have created vampires. Their power of synthesis allows them to kill a human host by infusing them with shadow potency, turning them into a vampire (possibly at the cost of their own &quot;life&quot;). Normally, the clan is same as the last vampire the embodied strix took vitae from or, in the case of a possessed revenant, the vampire who created the revenant.<br /> <br /> The book then says that a random clan is chosen if the host hasn't had any contact with vampires. I always found that to be a bit strange and meta, but whatever. What you could do is say that such a case of a mortal who's never been in contact with vampire blood and is the subject of the synthesis power results in a vampire without a clan. In my case, those vampires weren't so much clanless as they had unusual combinations of clan disciplines and weaknesses, making it impossible to say if they were from one particular clan or not. One of the PCs, who had only played masquerade, liked the idea of not having a clan, so I gave him that possibility (only revealing much later who/what his sire was). Until he met other &quot;clanless&quot; vampires (who were called &quot;orphans&quot; by other regular kindred), he pretty much introduced himself as gangrel since he had their weakness and the Resilience discipline (he also had Vigor and Celerity, so he could have said he was a Daeva too I guess). Basically, those random power and weakness distributions were an attempt by some strix to start the experiment over and create a new vampire breed who wouldn't be a failure like the first one.<br /> <br /> Or, and that might fit a self serving Dracula, why not a revenant who survived and became more and more powerful until he somehow managed to gain blood potency on his own, without outside help. Maybe he simply used his disciplines a lot and drank vampire blood and magic happened, or maybe that's the true origins of the Mysteries : a way to uplift oneself from revenant to kindred. Then, that particular mystery was lost because it's useless to a vampire and nobody really likes revenants enough to actually teach them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T13:11:31-08:00","id":1008656,"title":"","content":"Or he might have just started as a revenant and got by through sheer badassery for a while until he managed to diablerize a gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T13:47:14-08:00","id":1008668,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Dracula</b><br /> <br /> There is a difficulty in trying to depict Dracula, in that there have been <i>hundreds</i> (possibly thousands) of interpretations of the character in the over 100+years since the novel was published. Hell, even reading the novel one can come away with several different impressions about what the character represents, what his goals are, and the full extent of his powers.<br /> <br /> I recommend tailoring your Dracula based on what role he serves in the story and (especially in a RPG) where you want him to sit on power level. Going through a grocery list of specific tricks may not be the best use of time and energy, considering that if it comes down to a actual fight with PC's, most of those tricks won't get used and he will probably be dust in a few rounds.<br /> <br /> If you intend to make his abilities something that the players can use, take advantage of the toolkit nature of he game mechanics to develop a whole host of powers and abilities.<br /> <br /> And lastly, don't be too beholden to what was done in Masquerade. Its a great game, but its expectations and game mechanics are different enough from Requiem that converting material can be a lengthy and frustrating exercise. Instead, (if you intend on working with Requiem) get to know the mechanics and setting a little more. Work with the elements of the rules that the system is good at (for one, CofD is not quite as good at over-the-top swashbuckling combat, and its better for brutal acts of violence involving victims and perpetrators).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}